# Control for tools/check_light_filter.sh: a wall torch, a CLEAR cell, and a
# floor cell two steps from the torch behind it. The paired script
# light-ice-on.keys differs by one letter -- 'h' Ice Wall for 'e' Floor -- so
# the two runs measure the ice and nothing else.
#
# Terrain letters come from the wizard "Which terrain type?" list:
# [e] Floor, [h] Ice Wall, [p] Wall Torch.
#
# Placement runs far-to-near: the wizard's targeting cursor will not cross a
# solid cell, so the wall torch goes down last.
#
# The final UP/DOWN pair exists because ProbeDump only writes a block when the
# map, the player's position or the source count changes; a terrain edit alone
# changes none of the three.

@include chargen.keys
@dump:arrival

w y
@dump:wizard-menu

K RIGHT*3 ENTER e
w K RIGHT*2 ENTER e
w K UP ENTER e
w K RIGHT ENTER p

@dump:terrain-placed

UP
DOWN
@dump:measured

@quit
